# Fleet SSH trust — PUBLIC keys only, one per host. Safe to commit.
# Consumed by: Windows (provision/windows.ps1 -> administrators_authorized_keys,
# regenerated WHOLESALE) and POSIX (tier_ssh_trust -> ~/.ssh/authorized_keys,
# APPEND-ONLY).
#
# ⚠ REMOVING A LINE HERE DOES NOT REVOKE IT ON LINUX/macOS. tier_ssh_trust only
# appends keys it doesn't find; it never prunes. Windows does prune. So a
# retired key must ALSO be deleted by hand from ~/.ssh/authorized_keys on every
# POSIX member, or it stays trusted forever.
#
# ⚠ A REINSTALLED HOST GETS A NEW KEY AND NOTHING ADDS IT HERE AUTOMATICALLY.
# That is exactly how latitude locked itself out of desktop on 2026-08-01: the
# box was rebuilt as Debian, minted a new me@latitude, and this file still
# listed only its dead NixOS-era key. Update this file in the same change that
# rebuilds a host.
